  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Weapon Modification (requires melee weapon that deals slashing damage)</strong></p><p>Monomolecular edges, or \"mono-edges\", refer to blades that have been precision sharpened by lasers to the point where the cutting edge is measured in terms of molecules. In actuality, the term is more marketing than scientific, but the blades are still sharp enough to cause severe damage. However, the blades are also easy to dull and must be maintained.</p><p>Whenever you deal slashing damage with this weapon, you deal an additional 1d8 slashing damage. Once per turn, if you kill an enemy with an attack with this weapon, you may immediately make another attack with the same weapon against a different enemy within reach.</p>",
